course: dictionary
lesson: 7855
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «A girl in Michigan swam out to a raft in a lake; halfway she got tired and cold and went under.» The clues are the lake and swimming out to it, so a raft here is a flat floating platform that people can rest on.
explain: Read the words around the word and ask what would fit. «Sealed plastic bottles are full of air, so a raft of many bottles can hold up a child.» Here a raft is a platform, but a raft of many bottles can also mean a large number of bottles. Try each meaning in the sentence: only one of them makes sense as a platform that holds up a child.
explain: Raft can also be a verb, a doing word. To raft means to travel on a raft, especially down a river. Look at the ending: raft, rafts, rafted, rafting. If you see «rafting» in a story, the characters are probably on a river in a raft or a rubber boat.
fact: A raft is a flat floating platform, often made of logs, planks or barrels tied together.
fact: A raft can also be an inflatable rubber boat.
fact: A raft of things means a large number of them, as in «a raft of ideas».
fact: To raft means to travel on a raft, especially down a river, and this is called rafting.
exercise: «A girl in Michigan swam out to a raft in a lake; halfway she got tired and cold.» What is the raft? | *A floating platform for people to rest on | A kind of fish | A big rock on the shore | A type of swimming lesson
exercise: Mia says, «We are going rafting this summer.» What does rafting mean? | *Travelling on a raft, especially down a river | Swimming under the water | Sitting on the beach with a towel | Building a sandcastle
exercise: The teacher says, «We had a raft of questions after the talk.» What does a raft of questions mean? | A short, quiet question | *A large number of questions | A question with no answer | A boat made of questions
test: «The Mariner sits on his raft trailing his toes in the water.» What is the Mariner sitting on? | *A floating platform | A tall tree | A cave under the sea
test: Which word means travelling on a raft down a river? | climbing | walking | *rafting | singing
exam: Which meaning of raft fits «a raft of many bottles can hold up a child»? | To travel down a river | A large number of bottles | A rubber boat for games | *A flat floating platform
